Description: Experiment mode with isolated CPU cores for lab timing
 Experiment mode for lab computers with deterministic timing for EEG,
 button boxes and audio-visual stimuli. It adds GRUB entries with the
 kernel parameter experiment_mode=1, one set per CPU preset, that
 isolate CPU cores (isolcpus, nohz_full, rcu_nocbs) and keep the other
 IRQs off them (irqaffinity). The entries are made by update-grub
 itself, for every installed kernel. In experiment mode a service pins
 the IRQs of the sound cards (internal and USB) to the isolated cores,
 another one keeps services, virtual machines and login sessions off
 them, and irqbalance does not run. check-isolation and usb-affinity
 show the result.
 .
 Real-time IRQ priorities come from devjam-system-config-rtirq, which
 is installed with it. switch-rtirq chooses whether rtirq.service runs
 only in experiment mode or always (the default).

